  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Service-Disabled Veteran-Owned Small Business (SDVOSB) set-aside program obligated $8.1B in FY2026 to date. The program delivered 14,127 awards with an average award size of $572K, and obligations fell 6.9% year over year. Yearly obligations show program scale and variability: FY21 was $7.2B, FY22 was $8B, FY23 was $9.1B, FY24 was $8.8B, FY25 was $8.7B, and FY26 is $8.1B. The Department of Veterans Affairs dominated buying with $6.5B in obligations, while the Department of Defense obligated $765M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction and Other Computer Related Services are the largest NAICS categories with $2.4B and $1.7B respectively. Top vendor activity concentrated in a few firms: V3GATE, LLC received $515M and FOUR POINTS TECHNOLOGY, L.L.C. received $274M. These figures are contract obligations and reflect fiscal year to date totals, so current-year totals are partial. This summary highlights who bought the most, which industries captured the largest shares, and which vendors received the biggest SDVOSB set-aside awards.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are the biggest buyers of SDVOSB set-asides?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $6.5B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $765M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $143M. Other notable buyers include the Department of Transportation at $122M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $105M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors captured the most SDVOSB obligations?",
        "body": "Commercial and Institutional Building Construction captured $2.4B and Other Computer Related Services captured $1.7B in FY2026 to date. The largest vendor by obligations is V3GATE, LLC at $515M, followed by FOUR POINTS TECHNOLOGY, L.L.C. at $274M and SPREZZATURA MANAGEMENT CONSULTING, LLC at $214M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does the federal government award through SDVOSB set-asides?",
      "a": "The federal government awarded $8.1B through SDVOSB set-asides in FY2026 to date. Those obligations came through 14,127 awards with an average award size of $572K, and obligations fell 6.9% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations have ranged from $7.2B in FY21 to $9.1B in FY23 and $8.1B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies use SDVOSB set-asides the most?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs uses SDVOSB set-asides the most, obligating $6.5B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $765M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $143M, with other agencies like Transportation ($122M) and Health and Human Services ($105M) also active buyers."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest SDVOSB set-aside contractors?",
      "a": "The largest SDVOSB set-aside contractors by obligations in FY2026 to date are V3GATE, LLC at $515M, FOUR POINTS TECHNOLOGY, L.L.C. at $274M, and SPREZZATURA MANAGEMENT CONSULTING, LLC at $214M. Additional top vendors include HSGS-AMERESCO, LLC at $202M and IT CONCEPTS, INC. at $180M."
    }
